  "term": "Merkel’s corpuscle",
  "definition": "Merkel’s corpuscle is a specialized touch-sensitive nerve ending in the epidermis. It consists of the cup-shaped end of an intraepidermal axon that contacts the base of a single modified keratinocyte.",
